Description: GNOME app for zark backups
 Shows how zark's backups stand: how full the system pools are, each
 backup drive with its last backup, its space and its backup points by
 month, the datasets left out of backups, and a running backup with its
 progress.
 .
 It runs zark's operations (back up, reclaim space, prepare, check, erase
 and register drives, exclusions, retention): each is one zark command
 run through pkexec, with the administrator's password, in a terminal
 inside the window where zark asks its questions as it always does. The
 polkit policy gives each command its own action.
